! transmit_time_to_core.strap -- a TRANSMIT's time is set by where the
! words GO (docs/fidelity_plan.md A7, 2026-11-27).
!
! FIVE WORDS FROM INDEX STORAGE ($2-$6, words 18-22) TO CORE, immediate
! count.  Perf. Char. Vol. 1 Table 9 (printed p.3-14, PDF 32), T (XS ->
! EM): loop 3.0 us = 10 clocks a word, the same as EM -> EM; Vol. 2 PDF
! 107 (printed 100) measures I-BOX TO EXTERNAL at 10.05 clocks a word.
! The model charged the SOURCE read until A7: 2 clocks a word from index
! storage.  Its sibling transmit_time_to_index.strap moves five words the
! other way, core to index storage, where Table 9's loop is 4.2 us = 14
! clocks.  Between them, a model that charges the source (2 here, 10
! there) and one that charges the destination (10 here, 14 there) cannot
! give the same pair of counts.
!
! THE CYCLES PIN (tests/run_tests.sh) is the model's count for the whole
! deck, a model pin.  The transmit's part is bsv/StretchXmitTiming.bsv's
! charge, F + 5 L with F = 36 (TI into core) and L = 10.  Injections and
! their observed results are in run_tests.sh at the run.

        SLC, (8)2000.0
START   LVI, $X2, 11         ! something to move: value fields 11-15
        LVI, $X3, 12
        LVI, $X4, 13
        LVI, $X5, 14
        LVI, $X6, 15
        TI, 5, 18.0, DST         ! $2-$6 to DST..DST+4
        BEW, $

        SLC, (8)3000.0
DST     DD(BU,64), (16)FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
        DD(BU,64), (16)FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
        DD(BU,64), (16)FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
        DD(BU,64), (16)FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
        DD(BU,64), (16)FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
        DD(BU,64), (16)AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA   ! the fence: not written

        END, START
